    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0401" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794A.5/7–2350: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-23T15:00:00+09:00">July 23, 1950—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Delivered message to Foreign Minister Yeh this noon as instructed by Deptel 61, July 22.</p>
                <p>He requested me reply that Chinese Government intends observe its commitment,
                    that only violation has been unfortunate incident involving British ship<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d220-f1"/> for which Chinese Government offered apology and
                    compensation and that Chinese Government preparing <pb facs="0402" n="388"
                        xml:id="pg388"/> memorandum for ComSeventhFlt regarding Communist attacks on
                    small islands off mainland.</p>
                <p>Apart from foregoing, Yeh indicated Chinese Government considering withdrawal
                    from Chinmen despite “great importance to both China and US”. Plan calls for
                    mining of waters around Amoy and holding aircraft in readiness defend evacuation
                    in event Chinese Communist air force attempts intervene.</p>
                <p>Also passed to Yeh substance Deptel 55, July
                    21.</p>
                <p>Yesterday informed Chen Tai-Chu accordance Deptel 56, July 21<anchor n="2" xml:id="d220-f2"/> and reiterated
                    to Yeh today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="1" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>The incident referred to involved the strafing of the British motor vessel <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Glenearn</hi> by Chinese Nationalist Air Force planes on
                    July 15 resulting in the wounding of two crew members.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d220-f2" n="2" xml:id="d220-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 1 to telegram 74, July 17, from Taipei, <ref target="#pg381">p.
                        381</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
